  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $y=20^{301}$\r\nNumber of digits $=$ Integral part of\r\n$\\left(301 \\log _{10} 20\\right)+1$\r\nIntegral part of $\\left.\\left[301 \\log _{10} 10+\\log _{10} 2\\right)\\right]+1$\r\n$=$ Integral part of $[301(1+0.3010)]+1$\r\n$=$ Integral part of $[301 \\times 1.3010]+1$\r\nIntegral part of $[391.601]+1$\r\n$=391+1=392$",
